    <!-- No override="true". On an <fqname>-only <hal> it is a verified no-op:
         HalManifest::add()'s two override branches both die, because
         isDisabledHal() returns false as soon as forEachInstance yields and
         removeHals() iterates hal.versions, which parse_xml.cpp populates only
         from <version> children. Confirmed with this tree's assemble_vintf:
         byte-identical output either way. If a future SoC-common manifest ever
         needs to be beaten, add a real <version> child as well. -->
